Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:19:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/40] Switchers: close to where the window manager puts the
 windows

Picking a window in a scrolling workspace pans it at once, but
window.rect follows a frame or more later. The closing animation read the
old rects: a window just panned away still counted as on screen and its
card slid sideways after it, and the picked window faded instead of
growing into place. The switchers now take the window manager's own rect
(WINDOW_STATE_RECT) for where windows are before opening and after
closing.

The Window View (a subset of windows) also keeps the other windows on
screen and fades them out as it opens and back in as it closes, instead of
dropping them at once.
